                <pb facs="0394" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">365D.1163/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-23T09:00:00+03:00">December 23, 1936—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>692. My 690, December 22, 3 p.m. I have informed my British colleague of the
                    substance of my interview. He has had no intimation of the grounds assigned by
                    the authorities for their action.</p>
                <p>I am informed that one of the non-American letter writers is not even a member of
                    the mission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
